.TH WALLPAPER-SUITE-MANAGER 1 "November 2026" "Wallpaper Suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wallpaper-suite-manager \- serve Wallpaper Suite settings on the session bus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wallpaper-suite-manager
.br
.B wallpaper-suite-manager \-\-warm
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the Wallpaper Suite settings service for the current user session.
Settings clients normally request it through D-Bus activation using the name
.BR tech.norvi.WallpaperManager1 .
.PP
The service exposes typed display, library, rotation and diagnostic workflows.
Image processing uses separate workers. Wallpaper publication remains with
the enabled Wallpaper Suite GNOME Shell extension.
.PP
Running this command does not enable or install the extension.
.TP
.B \-\-warm
Index the configured library and prepare any missing library thumbnails and
per-display previews, then exit. The
.B wallpaper-suite-warm.timer
user unit runs this at idle priority after login and nightly; when nothing
changed it only checks the folder and cache.
.SH FILES
Manager request receipts are stored under
.BR $XDG_STATE_HOME/wallpaper-suite/ .
Prepared image assets use
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/wallpaper-suite/manager/ .
The usual XDG defaults apply when these variables are unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero after a normal session-bus shutdown, or one if startup fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wallpaper-suite (1),
.BR wallpaper-suitectl (1),
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
